      "headword_arabic": "سِتِّى",
      "definition": "A dialectal or vulgar vocative addressed to a woman, meaning “my lady” or “my mistress.”",
      "usage_conditions": "The expression is disputed in the lexical tradition: it is also explained through an interpretation involving the six surrounding positions, while some authorities regard it as incorrect or as a contraction of سَيِّدَتِي.",
